format: method/2
name: Produce and check the first iron plates
goal: Build a small production system in a fresh Factorio world and produce 20 new iron plates.
inputs:
  endpoint:
    type: text
    description: Local HTTP action endpoint for this test world.
  tool_documentation:
    type: text
    description: Absolute path to the allowed game action documentation.
environment:
  game:
    type: service
    description: A local Factorio test host with the fixed action API.
steps:
  produce:
    in:
      endpoint: inputs.endpoint
      tool_documentation: inputs.tool_documentation
      game: environment.game
    changes: [environment.game]
    do: |
      You are the playing agent. Read tool_documentation. Use only HTTP POSTs
      to endpoint for game observations and actions. Do not inspect game
      host code, host process arguments, credentials, run directories, saves,
      evaluator files, parent workspace files, or other game interfaces.
      Do not change repository files or commit anything. You may save the
      assigned output file and your own temporary action client in this step.

      Observe the starting world. Design your own plan to produce at least
      20 new iron plates in a furnace. Do not count initial inventory as new
      production. Execute the plan through the allowed actions, inspect the
      effects, and adapt when evidence shows a problem. Never assume that a
      failed request had no effect. Inspect before retrying an uncertain action.
      Use at most 120 requests and 12 minutes, including model thinking.
      Stop on timeout, loss of connection, or a host limit. Do not reset.

      Stop successfully when the game records at least 20 new iron plates,
      furnace products_finished confirms production, and furnace output holds
      at least 20 iron plates. Leave them there for the independent check.
      Save a short report with your initial plan, changes to it, actual actions,
      errors, starting and final observations, and the reason you stopped.
      Return an honest result even if you did not reach the goal.
    out:
      report:
        type: file
        format: markdown
        description: Plan, actions, errors, game observations, and stop reason.
      completed:
        type: boolean
        description: Whether the game evidence shows the production goal was met.
    check: |
      Read report. Do not play or repair the game. Make one observe request to
      endpoint. Confirm that completed is true, the game's iron_plates_produced
      is at least 20, furnace products_finished sums to at least 20, and furnace
      output contains at least 20 iron plates. Confirm the report supplies a
      starting observation with zero iron plate production. An agent's claim
      alone is not proof. Return fail for missing production or ambiguous if
      the game cannot be inspected. Use only the supplied HTTP endpoint and
      report; do not inspect host files or other interfaces.
result:
  completed: completed
  report: report
